- Assumptions: above the stock box, Careful 6%, Middle 7% (ours) and Hopeful 8%, and above inflation 2.5%, 3% (ours) and 4%, with one line on what the forecasters expect (4.8%-6.8% Vanguard, 7.5% J.P. Morgan, October 2026) and every reason in the sources fold; a link from Will the money last? opens that one number with its own Save, the rest under "All the numbers"; saving a changed figure says what it did to the retirement answer ("now runs out at 69 (was 70)"), a stock return above 8% gets an amber "Higher than any forecast we know; plan on it only if you have a reason", and Will the money last? then says it rests "on your hopeful return"; opened from the menu, Assumptions shows how fast prices rise and stocks grow first with one "Save", the other eight under "All the numbers" (opening it makes Save "Save and mark as reviewed"), and a save names what moved ("Saved: prices rising 3% → 4%").
